nk the  important point that she made that  really is critical  was the two opposing forces because she  was trying to get  information into the president on a  regular basis but  the president was getting information  from other sources you know  friends on the outside who would call  him up or people who would  who would have input into it and that  gradually attenuated her influence to  the point where she didn't really see  him very much anymore  that's what she was trying to explain  right you said the one million doses per  day  in the first 100 days was a floor not a  ceiling  just doing some simple arithmetic myself  to get to 70 to 85 percent  vaccinated americans by the end of the  summer early fall we would need to be at  about twice the rate  we currently are at 1 million a day and  the goal of the biden administration  so when you talk about a ceiling is 2  million a day plus  is that possible based on what you see  so far  no i think it is you know if you listen  to what the president said he said we're  going to try and get as many doses into  people  as we possibly can as quickly as we can  he set a goal  a little bit ago and and you know  hopefully we'll meet and  surpass that goal that's the point i  mean  is it only just because someone gives  just be i hope hope is not i just i  hope is an odd thing to lean on at this  point i mean can we do it  do we have the the manufacturing coming  online do the executive orders from last  week the defense production act does  that  help us reach that goal and and how  yes yes and yes yes we can reach it  he set an original goal of a hundred  million doses in the first hundred days  and as i've said and others have said  that's a floor  not a ceiling it's a reasonable goal  it's not you know it's not easy  to get doses from where you go in the  vial  all through the transportation into  people's arms particularly  when you get out of the realm of giving  it in a hospital  or giving it a nursing home and you've  got to go out into the community  particularly  underserved communities to get it to  people so if people think that's easy  it's not  it gets hard and it'll get harder do we  think we can do it  absolutely we think we can do it let's  touch on the travel ban because the  reporting we have is that today the  biden administration joe biden himself  will announce restrictions on travelers  coming into the u.s from uh the uk and  also crucially south africa where there  is a  mutation that uh scientists are  concerned about  how effective do you think a travel ban  will be  given we recall president trump  instituted a travel ban on china  and it didn't seem to work out too well  well first of all it clearly will be  helpful we  we have concern about the mutation  that's in south africa we're looking at  it very actively  it is clearly a different and more  ominous than the one  in the uk and i think it's very prudent  to restrict travel of non-citizens but  there's also  something else that we didn't have  before is that people coming into the  country are going to be required  to have a test before they get on the  plane  when they get off the plane and land  here they're going to have to have  a quarantine as well as a second test  if i can give you a touch of good news  as you go dr fouchon we appreciate you  coming  spring training starts in three weeks  baseball season is on its way  thank you very much yes thank you  thanks a lot good to be with you
 

